WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.460
- Captain's Log, final entry

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.920
Spock and I are the sole survivors

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:11.120
Enterprise, are you there?

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:15.000
- Good morning, Wendy

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:15.780
- Good morning, Scotty

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.980
- Can we go over your everyday schedule?

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.480
- Wake up, go to work

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:21.680
Welcome to Cinnabon, would you like a Cinnabon?

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.060
- How's your script coming?

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.660
- I just wrote a story where Spock travels to Deep Space 9

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:26.780
- That sounds awesome

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:29.540
- 3PM: Take Pete for a walk

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.580
- 6PM: Watch Star Trek before I go to bed

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.180
- Send in your script highlighting the best of the Star Trek universe

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.540
- Next week, your sister's coming

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:40.620
- There's a Star Trek script writing contest

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.560
We can go to the post office,

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:42.920
and then I can go home with you

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:45.360
Can you please tell Audrey that I'm ready to go home now?

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:46.900
- Please stand by

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:47.540
Breathe

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:52.300
- Your completed script must be received by February 16th

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:53.080
- Where are you going?

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:53.840
- Los Angeles

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.960
Bus driver: my friend needs to pee

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.440
Don't do it, Pete!

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:01.500
This is what happens when you pee on the bus

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.440
- Me and my boyfriend, we're actually going down to L.A.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:06.860
Maybe you should just come with us

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.900
- She's 5 foot 4, blonde

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:09.540
- That's her

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.420
- I know he's the hero of Star Wars,

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.440
but who exactly is this Kirk person?

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:15.780
- She's out there, alone

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.260
- She's a very resourceful girl

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:20.180
- GIVE ME MY NOTEBOOK BACK!

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:22.240
Where am I?

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.900
- You're at the hospital, you hit your head

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:25.100
- She jumped out the window!

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.560
- How did she get away from you people?

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:31.000
- (foreign language)

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.460
- (foreign language)

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:33.400
- What language is that?

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:34.380
- It's Klingon

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:39.300
- Your sister is one of the most complex

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.760
and creative people I know

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:43.920
- People have their own lives,

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.780
and after awhile, those lives don't include you

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.160
- Captain, there is only one logical direction in which to go

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:51.340
Forward

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.280
- Light: it can travel for millions of years

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:02.340
before finally reaching its destination

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:04.480
Do you know how hard it is to write something?

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:06.720
Because the story you want to tell means so much to you?

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:08.260
It goes lonely and alone,

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:09.940
hoping that it will reach someone

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.380
- That's amazing

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:12.500
So, what happens next?

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.720
- The unknown is there for us to conquer,

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:15.740
not to fear

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.080
- What was Leonard McCoy's daughter's name?

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:20.700
- Joanna

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:21.840
- Oh, snap!

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:22.420
- Pay up!

